// Title: Potential DLL Sideloading Via DeviceEnroller.EXE
// Sigma ID: e173ad47-4388-4012-ae62-bd13f71c18a8
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: @gott_cyber
// Date: 2022-08-29 | Modified: 2023-02-04
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects the use of the PhoneDeepLink parameter to potentially sideload a DLL file that does not
//   exist. This non-existent DLL file is named "ShellChromeAPI.dll". Adversaries can drop their own
//   renamed DLL and execute it via DeviceEnroller.exe using this parameter
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://mobile.twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1564131230941122561
//   - https://strontic.github.io/xcyclopedia/library/DeviceEnroller.exe-24BEF0D6B0ECED36BB41831759FDE18D.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_deviceenroller_dll_sideloading.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\deviceenroller.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "deviceenroller.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains "/PhoneDeepLink"
